p['urgent_extra']='Call your oncology team immediately for a temperature of 37.5°C or above, 36°C or below, shivering or suddenly feeling unwell. Infection can occur without a fever. Call urgently for bleeding, severe diarrhoea, repeated vomiting, inability to drink, very little urine or new breathlessness. Severe breathing difficulty, heavy bleeding or collapse needs 112 / 999.'
p['teachback']='Can you show the two five-day dosing blocks and the rest days, explain how you take tablets with meals, what you do after a missed or vomited dose, and how you get urgent help?'
p['consent_support']='Discuss the disease-control aim, expected benefit and uncertainty, alternatives including supportive care without this treatment, infection/bleeding risk, bowel symptoms and dehydration, oral dosing responsibilities, kidney/liver suitability, fertility, pregnancy prevention and your right to reconsider.'
p['questions']+= [dict(q='What if I miss a dose or vomit?',a='Do not make up a missed, held or vomited dose and do not double the next dose. Tell your team and follow the next scheduled dose on the agreed calendar. Repeated vomiting needs advice because of dehydration and missed medicines.'),dict(q='Are tablet-free days safe days?',a='No. The rest period allows recovery, but low blood counts and other problems can occur then too. Use the same urgent contact plan throughout the cycle.'),dict(q='Can my morning and evening tablet numbers differ?',a='Yes. The pharmacy may prescribe different morning and evening quantities to match the correct total daily dose. Do not assume the same number or substitute tablet strengths; follow the written label and calendar.'),dict(q='Is the bevacizumab combination evidence the same?',a='No. A study of Lonsurf plus bevacizumab tests an additional medicine and its extra risks. Its results should not be presented as the expected benefit of Lonsurf on its own.')]
p['support']=[item('A written tablet calendar',p['administration_text'],['nccp','smpc']),item('Prevent and treat sickness','This oral medicine has moderate-to-high sickness risk. Agree a preventive and rescue anti-sickness plan with the team. If you cannot keep fluids or medicines down, call; do not add or repeat doses yourself.',['nccp','oral-antiemetic']),item('Food, fluids and bowel symptoms','Take tablets after meals as instructed. Drink as your team advises and report diarrhoea, repeated vomiting, poor intake or reduced urine early. A prescribed bowel treatment plan does not replace urgent assessment.',['smpc']),item('Blood tests and infection','Blood count, kidney/liver tests and urine-protein checks occur before treatment and each cycle; extra tests may be needed, especially with kidney impairment. Report fever or illness even on rest days.',['nccp','smpc']),item('Pregnancy prevention','Discuss fertility before treatment. Women need highly effective contraception during treatment and for six months after; add a barrier method to hormonal contraception. Men with a partner who could become pregnant need effective contraception during treatment and for six months afterwards. Do not breastfeed while taking this medicine.',['nccp','smpc'])]
